# Lab 20: Add one companion for a selected GCP agent
#
# This demo requires two demo-specific decisions before it starts:
#
# A365_DEMO_TARGET_NAME=<exact-GCP-package-display-name>
# A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_GROUP=<approved-blueprint-group-label>
#
# A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_OBJECT_ID is optional. Set it only when protected local
# mapping identifies an approved reusable Blueprint for this group.
# Leave it empty when no Blueprint has been approved yet; Part 1 then provides
# a separately gated creation path.
#
# Shared authentication remains in the Lab 20 root .env:
#
# A365_TENANT_ID=<directory-tenant-id>
# A365_CLIENT_ID=<public-client-application-id>
#
# Before Prep 1, open ../../.env and set:
#
# A365_DEMO_TARGET_NAME=<exact displayName of the selected GCP agent>
# A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_GROUP=<approved Blueprint group label>
#
# Choose the GCP agent in advance and copy its name exactly, including spaces
# and capitalization. The group is the approved credential and
# governance boundary; it is not derived from the Package name.
#
# The helper derives the Package ID, exact provider source ID, and source
# timestamps from read-only Package responses. The create responses supply the
# Blueprint app ID, Agent Identity ID, and companion Registration ID.
#
# Run one request at a time. Never use "Send All".
#
# Save private responses only under:
# ../../evidence/demos/01-add-companion/
#
# The normal order is:
#
#   Discovery -> Part 1 Blueprint -> Part 2 Identity -> Part 3 Registration
#
# Parts 1, 2, and 3 contain separately gated POST requests. Never repeat any
# POST after a success, timeout, 5xx, or another ambiguous outcome. Reconcile
# protected local state before deciding whether another write is safe.
#
# Required delegated Microsoft Graph permissions:
# - User.Read
# - CopilotPackages.Read.All
# - AgentIdentityBlueprint.Read.All
# - AgentIdentityBlueprint.Create (Part 1 creation branch only)
# - AgentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal.Read.All
# - AgentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal.Create (Part 1 creation branch only)
# - AgentIdentity.Read.All
# - AgentIdentity.Create.All (Part 2 only)
# - AgentRegistration.Read.All
# - AgentRegistration.ReadWrite.All (Part 3 only)
#
# Never commit .env, mapping.json, token responses, raw responses, screenshots
# containing identifiers, or generated Agent 365 configuration.

@tenantId = {{$dotenv A365_TENANT_ID}}
@clientId = {{$dotenv A365_CLIENT_ID}}
@targetName = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_TARGET_NAME}}
@blueprintGroup = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_GROUP}}
@blueprintObjectId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_OBJECT_ID}}
@blueprintAppId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_APP_ID}}
@originalPackageId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_ORIGINAL_PACKAGE_ID}}
@providerSourceAgentId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID}}
@sourceCreatedAt = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_SOURCE_CREATED_AT}}
@sourceModifiedAt = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_SOURCE_MODIFIED_AT}}
@graphBaseUrl = https://graph.microsoft.com
@demoScopes = https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FUser.Read%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FCopilotPackages.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentityBlueprint.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentityBlueprint.Create%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal.Create%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentity.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentity.Create.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentRegistration.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentRegistration.ReadWrite.All%20offline_access

###############################################################################
# Prep 1 - Request a device code
#
# Expected: 200. Copy user_code, open verification_uri, and complete sign-in.
# Never save this response.

# @name demoStartDeviceCode
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/devicecode
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id={{clientId}}&scope={{demoScopes}}

###

###############################################################################
# Prep 2 - Exchange the device code
#
# Send only after browser sign-in is complete. Expected: 200.
# If authorization_pending is returned, wait for the interval from Prep 1.
# Never save this response.

# @name demoToken
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Agrant-type%3Adevice_code&client_id={{clientId}}&device_code={{demoStartDeviceCode.response.body.$.device_code}}

###

###############################################################################
# Prep 3 - Confirm the signed-in operator
#
# Expected: 200.
# Keep the returned user ID private.

# @name demoCurrentUser
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/me?$select=id
Authorization: Bearer {{demoToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Discovery 1 - Read the complete inventory and select one GCP Package
#
# Expected: 200. Save this response as:
#
# ../../evidence/demos/01-add-companion/package-list.json
#
# In most cases, this is the only file needed. Check the saved response for
# @odata.nextLink:
#
# - If @odata.nextLink is absent, the list is complete. Run:
#
# python demos/01-add-companion/prepare_demo.py select
#
# - If @odata.nextLink is present, the server has split the Package list into
#   pages. Send a GET request to that exact URL, save the response as
#   package-list-2.json, and repeat until the latest response has no
#   @odata.nextLink. Then pass every saved page to the helper, for example:
#
# python demos/01-add-companion/prepare_demo.py select --package-list evidence/demos/01-add-companion/package-list.json evidence/demos/01-add-companion/package-list-2.json
#
# The helper requires exactly one GoogleVertexAI Package whose displayName
# equals A365_DEMO_TARGET_NAME. It first prints safe Package counts grouped by
# returned platform, then writes only
# A365_DEMO_ORIGINAL_PACKAGE_ID to the ignored .env and prints no identifier.

# @name demoListPackages
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
Authorization: Bearer {{demoToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Discovery 2 - Read and parse the selected Package
#
# Restart or reload REST Client after the helper changes .env if this request
# still shows an unresolved originalPackageId.
#
# Expected: 200. Confirm displayName is A365_DEMO_TARGET_NAME and platform is
# GoogleVertexAI. Save the response as:
#
# ../../evidence/demos/01-add-companion/package-details.json
#
# Then run:
#
# python demos/01-add-companion/prepare_demo.py prepare
#
# The helper parses the nested definition JSON and writes these generated
# values to the ignored .env:
#
# - A365_DEMO_ORIGINAL_PACKAGE_ID
# - A365_DEMO_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID
# - A365_DEMO_SOURCE_CREATED_AT
# - A365_DEMO_SOURCE_MODIFIED_AT
#
# It rejects a non-GCP Package, a name mismatch, multiple source definitions,
# a missing source timestamp, or an original Package that already has an
# Agent Identity.

# @name demoGetSelectedPackage
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{originalPackageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{demoToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Part 1.1A - Reuse a recorded platform Blueprint
#
# Use this branch only when A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_OBJECT_ID came from protected
# local mapping for GoogleVertexAI/A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_GROUP.
# Expected: 200. A 403, 404, or mismatch is a stop condition; it is not
# permission to create a replacement.
#
# Save a successful response as:
#
# ../../evidence/demos/01-add-companion/blueprint.json
#
# Skip this request when A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_OBJECT_ID is empty.

# @name demoGetExistingBlueprint
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/applications/{{blueprintObjectId}}/microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprint
Authorization: Bearer {{demoToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Stop 1A - Approve creation of one group Blueprint
#
# Reach this gate only when:
# - Discovery confirmed GoogleVertexAI inventory;
# - A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_GROUP names the approved credential boundary;
# - protected mapping contains no reusable Blueprint for that group;
# - no earlier Blueprint POST has an unresolved outcome; and
# - creating one disposable Blueprint is explicitly authorized.
#
# If a reusable Blueprint was read in Part 1.1A, skip Part 1.1B.

###############################################################################
# Part 1.1B - Create the approved platform Blueprint
#
# DO NOT SEND THIS REQUEST until Stop 1A is satisfied.
# Expected: 201. On timeout, 5xx, or another unexpected response, stop and do
# not retry. Save a successful response as:
#
# ../../evidence/demos/01-add-companion/blueprint.json

# @name demoCreateBlueprint
POST {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/applications/microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprint
Authorization: Bearer {{demoToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "displayName": "GoogleVertexAI - {{blueprintGroup}} - disposable Blueprint",
  "sponsors@odata.bind": [
    "{{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/users/{{demoCurrentUser.response.body.$.id}}"
  ],
  "owners@odata.bind": [
    "{{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/users/{{demoCurrentUser.response.body.$.id}}"
  ]
}

###

###############################################################################
# Part 1.2 - Resolve one Blueprint result into local state
#
# After either Part 1.1A or Part 1.1B succeeds, save that one response as
# blueprint.json and run from the Lab 20 directory:
#
# python demos/01-add-companion/prepare_demo.py blueprint
#
# The helper validates the response and writes both generated identifiers:
#
# - A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_OBJECT_ID
# - A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_APP_ID
#
# Restart or reload REST Client after the helper changes .env.

###############################################################################
# Part 1.3 - Re-read the resolved Blueprint
#
# Expected: 200. Overwrite blueprint.json with this verified response.

# @name demoGetBlueprint
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/applications/{{blueprintObjectId}}/microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprint
Authorization: Bearer {{demoToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Part 1.4 - Look for the matching Blueprint principal
#
# Expected: 200 when the principal already exists, or 404 when it is genuinely
# absent. A 403 or another error is a stop condition.

# @name demoGetBlueprintPrincipal
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals(appId='{{blueprintAppId}}')/microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal
Authorization: Bearer {{demoToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Stop 1B - Approve creation of the Blueprint principal
#
# Send Part 1.5 only after Part 1.4 returned a definite 404, protected state
# contains no unresolved principal creation, and one create is authorized.
# Skip Part 1.5 when Part 1.4 returned 200.

###############################################################################
# Part 1.5 - Create the missing Blueprint principal
#
# DO NOT SEND THIS REQUEST after a successful principal read.
# Expected: 201. On timeout, 5xx, or another unexpected response, stop and do
# not retry.

# @name demoCreateBlueprintPrincipal
POST {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals/microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal
Authorization: Bearer {{demoToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "appId": "{{blueprintAppId}}"
}

###

###############################################################################
# Part 1.6 - Verify the Blueprint principal
#
# Run after either an existing principal returned 200 or Part 1.5 returned 201.
# Expected: 200. Confirm appId equals A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_APP_ID and
# accountEnabled is not false. Save the response as:
#
# ../../evidence/demos/01-add-companion/blueprint-principal.json

# @name demoVerifyBlueprintPrincipal
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals(appId='{{blueprintAppId}}')/microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal
Authorization: Bearer {{demoToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Stop 2 - Approve one Agent Identity creation
#
# Continue only when all of the following are true:
# - the selected Package and exact provider source are disposable and approved;
# - the platform Blueprint and enabled principal were verified;
# - the approved group contains this selected GCP agent;
# - no Agent Identity or unresolved earlier identity POST exists for this
#   provider source; and
# - one Agent Identity creation attempt is explicitly authorized.

###############################################################################
# Part 2.1 - Create the dedicated Agent Identity
#
# DO NOT SEND THIS REQUEST until Stop 2 is satisfied.
#
# Expected: 201. The signed-in operator is the required sponsor.
# On timeout, 5xx, or another unexpected response, stop and do not retry.
# Save a successful response as:
#
# ../../evidence/demos/01-add-companion/agent-identity.json

# @name demoCreateAgentIdentity
POST {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals/microsoft.graph.agentIdentity
Authorization: Bearer {{demoToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "displayName": "{{targetName}} - managed Agent Identity",
  "agentIdentityBlueprintId": "{{blueprintAppId}}",
  "sponsors@odata.bind": [
    "{{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/users/{{demoCurrentUser.response.body.$.id}}"
  ]
}

###

###############################################################################
# Part 2.2 - Verify the created Agent Identity
#
# Run only after Part 2.1 returned 201.
# Expected: 200. Overwrite agent-identity.json with this verified response.
# Confirm:
# - id is unchanged from the POST response;
# - agentIdentityBlueprintId equals the Blueprint appId; and
# - servicePrincipalType is ServiceIdentity.

# @name demoGetNewAgentIdentity
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals/{{demoCreateAgentIdentity.response.body.$.id}}/microsoft.graph.agentIdentity
Authorization: Bearer {{demoToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Stop 3 - Approve one companion Registration creation
#
# Continue only when:
# - the verified Agent Identity belongs to the approved Blueprint;
# - no active companion mapping exists for this provider source;
# - no unresolved earlier Registration POST exists for this source; and
# - one Registration creation attempt is explicitly authorized.
#
# There is no supported Agent Registration collection/list operation. The
# absence check therefore depends on protected durable mapping and experiment
# history; it must not be guessed from a failed GET using another identifier.

###############################################################################
# Part 3.1 - Create the companion Registration
#
# DO NOT SEND THIS REQUEST until Stop 3 is satisfied.
#
# The POST combines the three inputs established by the design:
# 1. Blueprint app ID from Part 1
# 2. Agent Identity ID from Part 2
# 3. deterministic companion source ID derived from the exact provider source
#
# Expected: 201. On timeout, 5xx, or another unexpected response, stop and do
# not retry. Save a successful response as:
#
# ../../evidence/demos/01-add-companion/companion-registration.json

# @name demoCreateFreshCompanion
POST {{graphBaseUrl}}/beta/copilot/agentRegistrations
Authorization: Bearer {{demoToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
OData-Version: 4.0

{
  "displayName": "{{targetName}} - managed companion",
  "description": "Disposable independently managed companion registration",
  "createdBy": "{{demoCurrentUser.response.body.$.id}}",
  "ownerIds": [
    "{{demoCurrentUser.response.body.$.id}}"
  ],
  "sourceAgentId": "agent-governance:companion:v1:gcp:{{providerSourceAgentId}}",
  "originatingStore": "GoogleVertexAI",
  "sourceCreatedDateTime": "{{sourceCreatedAt}}",
  "sourceLastModifiedDateTime": "{{sourceModifiedAt}}",
  "agentIdentityBlueprintId": "{{blueprintAppId}}",
  "agentIdentityId": "{{demoCreateAgentIdentity.response.body.$.id}}"
}

###

###############################################################################
# Part 3.2 - Verify the created companion
#
# Run only after Part 3.1 returned 201.
# Expected: 200. Overwrite companion-registration.json with this verified
# response and confirm all three inputs match.

# @name demoGetNewCompanion
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/beta/copilot/agentRegistrations/{{demoCreateFreshCompanion.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{demoToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json
OData-Version: 4.0

###

###############################################################################
# Part 4 - Re-read the original Registry Sync Package
#
# Expected: 200. Confirm the original Package still has no agentIdentityId.
# A successful companion does not enrich or replace the inventory Package.

# @name demoGetOriginalPackageAfter
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{originalPackageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{demoToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Finalize - Persist the mapping for rename and delete
#
# After saving the verified Blueprint, Blueprint principal, Agent Identity, and
# Registration responses at the paths above, run:
#
# python demos/01-add-companion/prepare_demo.py finalize
#
# The helper verifies the Blueprint -> Identity -> Registration relationships,
# saves the ignored durable mapping at:
#
# ../../evidence/demos/01-add-companion/mapping.json
#
# and updates these generated values in the ignored .env:
#
# - A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_APP_ID
# - A365_DEMO_AGENT_IDENTITY_ID
# - A365_DEMO_COMPANION_REGISTRATION_ID
#
# Rename and delete use those persisted values. Do not erase the mapping if a
# later lifecycle step is partial or fails.
